<title>CANADA: Rogers Communications Q4 net loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Rogers Communications Q4 net loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996		     1995</p>
<p> Shr	   Loss	C$0.20     Loss	C$0.44</p>
<p> Net	   Loss	28,318     Loss	67,099</p>
<p> Revs		     655,603		  593,631</p>
<p>		  YEAR</p>
<p> Shr	   Loss	C$1.72     Loss	C$1.78</p>
<p> Net	   Loss     278,370     Loss     283,357</p>
<p> Revs		   2,482,953		2,196,043</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 178,080		  177,614</p>
<p>     (All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>Note: Full-year 1996 earnings include a C$25 million gain on the sale of associated company. Fourth quarter results included a C$36.4 million on the sale of some cable television systems and a C$27.6 million gain on the issue of warrants by a subsidiary to a minority shareholder.</p>
<p>Full-year 1995 includes C$152.6 million writedown and share of losses of Unitel Communications Holdings Inc and a C$34 million write-down of the company's investment in Claircom Communications Group Inc.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
